/>

### What if I don't qualify?

<AccessException />

## Connecting

The P1 NGC HPC is air-gapped. Access needs multi-factor authentication and the Omnissa Remote
Desktop client, and you get instructions once registered. From the remote desktop,
`ssh -X <your-username>@login` reaches the login node.

Useful hosts:

```text
https://console.cld076.vmc/status   # Internal status page
cld076-0004.cld076.vmc              # Internal SFTP
sftp.spc.ngc.dk                     # External Ingress/Egress (SFTP)
```

## Using the Cluster

The cluster runs PBS, and `iqsub` opens a quick interactive session. Jobs name your project's
group and account, which you get when access is approved. Scheduler flags are in NGC's internal
documentation, linked from the status page.

The cluster has no internet access, so `git clone` from a public forge, `pip install` and `conda`
do not work. Code, data, packages and results pass through the SFTP staging area at `/data/upload`
under admin supervision, and anything leaving needs your NGC admin's approval. Ask your NGC admin
for access to `/data/upload` as your project's data gateway.

The gallery shows how to move [code, data and dependencies](/gallery/xfr-dat/) through the staging
area. See [every example that runs on P1 NGC HPC](/gallery/?provider=ngc).

## Policy & Support

### What are the limits?

<ClusterQuotas slug="ngc" />

- Only use this GDPR-compliant cluster for projects that need it
- Each project needs a signed Data Processing Agreement naming NGC as data processor
- High-risk projects also need a DPIA

### How much storage do I get?

Your quota is set when your project is onboarded. The staging area at `/data/upload` is a gateway
only. Clear your files from it once they have landed, so the next transfer does not compete with
them.

Your Data Processing Agreement governs retention, and personal data may not stay once the project
ends. Agree deletion or archiving with your NGC admin and the compute coordinator well before
then.

